Z||000004||Cliff Pennock||08-30-2000||12:57 PM||||0-60 in 13s is way too slow for an 88GT. I do agree however that weight makes a big difference. My 86.5GT does 0-60 in 9.2s and even that is too slow.||||reg||1
Z||000005||yobtah||08-30-2000||01:13 PM||||Driver ability plays a *huge* part in acceleration times also.  It's especially important if you're driving a manual transmission car.  Your shift speed and the rpm point you choose for shifting could easily add a few seconds to your 0-60 time.  The 2.8 typically runs out of breath beyond 5000 or 5500 rpm.  If you hold a gear past that point, you'll slow your time.  On the other hand, if you shift early, you'll miss the power peak, and lose time again.  You'll also enter the next gear with rpms too low, and you'll lose time running up to the power peak in that gear.||||reg||1
